  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive (0.00–0.50) to account for mean reversion and underestimation bias.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (e.g., >70.00) by 5–10% to avoid overreaction to short-term volatility.",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1–2 days when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25) to reflect delayed market correction.",
    "Apply a downward bias correction if true outcomes consistently fall below 30-day forecasts, especially when sentiment is flat or mildly positive.",
    "Avoid overfitting to recent highs; use 18-day history as anchor for smoothing, not 30-day forecast horizon."
  ]
}
